 :consensus-impact-note "Zero wire-protocol breaking changes or flag-day upgrades. All changes are node-local: structural Core-State vs Value-Aware Local Cache split (bitecho.cache.core), crash-safe extract-before-compact migration with ENOSPC fail-closed guardrails, BIP-022 backup Core-State-only boundary, Browser IndexedDB v2 upgrade with Closure-safe accessors, full-node O(1) snapshot retention caps, off-heap GC hysteresis/backoff, hot-LRU hysteresis & scan-resistant admission, 5s SIGTERM hard-exit watchdog, rotate-1 --events-out with inode-aware wait-event tailing, and storage/latency telemetry in bitecho.status/v1 and /statusz."
